    "title": "VIDEO: No. 13-ranked Angelo State Rams will kick off the 2025 season Thursday night - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Charles Bryce ,\n46 minutes ago\nSAN ANGELO, Texas ( Concho Valley Homepage ) — The No. 13-ranked Angelo State University football team will look to avenge last year’s season-opening loss against Fort Hays State when the Rams kick off the 2025 season Thursday night in Hays, Kansas.\nKickoff for the non-conference matchup is scheduled for 7 p.m. at Lewis Field Stadium.\nThe Tigers beat the Rams 21-7 last year at home in the first-ever meeting between ASU and Fort Hays.\nASU went 9-3 overall and 9-0 in the Lone Star Conference a year ago, and the Rams were upset at home by Bemidji State in the first round of the NCAA Division II playoffs.\nFort Hays finished 8-3 overall and a perfect 6-0 at home in 2024.\nRams junior quarterback Braeden Fuller was named the LSC Preseason Offensive Player of the Year for 2025. He was a Harlon Hill Award finalist for the best player in D-II last year, in addition to being the LSC’s Offensive Player of the Year.\nFuller led the LSC with 2,318 yards passing and 19 touchdowns, in addition to rushing for 10 scores and 678 yards.\nClick on the video above to hear what Coach Girsch had to say earlier this week about the season opener.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ConchoValleyHomepage.com.",
